# openrc-strip.list — v26 SLIM open-init strip manifest (v25 + stock web stack)
#
# Paths (rootfs-relative, NO leading slash) removed by openrc-assemble.sh from
# the unsquashed $FS BEFORE mksquashfs. Lines beginning with # and blank lines
# are ignored. `rm -rf` is tolerant of already-absent paths.
#
# Every path below was resolved against the br-0050 base-rootfs reference
# (/home/guillaume/.claude/jobs/5eb9adaf/tmp/base-rootfs) and ONLY listed if it
# EXISTS there. Each "verify-only-used-by" library was confirmed via a full
# DT_NEEDED reverse-dependency scan of the entire rootfs (needed-map.txt).
#
# DO-NOT-REMOVE invariant (must never appear here): libbwdpi.so libbwdpi_sql.so
# libsqlite3.so* libovpn.so libssl.so.1.1 libcrypto.so.1.1 /lib/modules/*/extra
# cfg80211.ko wl hostapd* nvram eapd wlceventd mcpd acsd2 wlconf ethswctl vlanctl
# fc/fcctl bcm_boot_launcher rc /rom/etc/rc3.d dropbearmulti sftp-server
# openrc-init* OpenRC libs.
#
# ===========================================================================
# SOURCE-PROVENANCE DISPOSITION (feat/openssl3-and-pkg-trim, 2026-06-08)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Q: can these strips be done at the SOURCE (don't-build) instead of post-build?
# A: NO, for almost all of them. The open-init base rootfs (br-0050 / blob 0035)
#    is NOT assembled from Buildroot packages. It is the MONOLITHIC merlin blob
#    `gt-be98-rootfs-<ver>.tar.gz` (package/gt-be98-rootfs), consumed VERBATIM by
#    board/gt-be98/post-image-full.sh (see configs/gt-be98_full_defconfig:
#    BR2_INIT_NONE, no busybox, only BR2_PACKAGE_GT_BE98_ROOTFS + _BOOTFS + the
#    /usr/br island pkgs). rootfs-transform.sh only (a) deletes rootfs-remove.list
#    paths, (b) overlays rootfs-overlay-full/, (c) harvests the /usr/br island.
#    Therefore every component below is CATEGORY (iii) — baked into the opaque
#    proprietary blob, removable ONLY post-build — EXCEPT the /usr/br island:
#
#  (i)  BUILDROOT PACKAGE, source-disable possible:  NONE.
#       No BR2_PACKAGE_SAMBA/TOR/OPENVPN/STRONGSWAN/MINIDLNA/NETATALK/LIGHTTPD/
#       WIREGUARD/etc. is selected in ANY open-init-lineage defconfig (full /
#       openrc-init / fromsrc / pkgtest / inverted). They are NOT built here.
#       (The OLD granular configs/gt-be98_defconfig DOES select buildroot
#       OPENVPN/STRONGSWAN/LIGHTTPD/OPENSSL + gt-be98-samba + -userspace-base,
#       but that is a SEPARATE, non-open-init lineage — out of scope, untouched.)
#
#  (ii) MERLIN PREBUILT harvested by rootfs-transform — the /usr/br block ONLY:
#       usr/br/bin/{openssl,ssh,ssh-keygen} are BUILT FROM SOURCE
#       (gt-be98-br-openssl 3.6.2 static CLI; gt-be98-br-openssh ssh/ssh-keygen
#       clients), harvested into the rootfs by rootfs-transform.sh, then stripped
#       here = genuine build-then-harvest-then-strip waste. They are NOT removed
#       at source because: (1) gt-be98-br-openssl's static dev-tree
#       (libcrypto.a) is REQUIRED to statically link gt-be98-br-openssh, so the
#       PACKAGE must stay; (2) the harvest + this strip list both feed the
#       COMMITTED, gate-validated br-0050 base shared by gt-be98_full_defconfig —
#       editing the shared harvest perturbs that baseline. Pruning these from the
#       harvest is a documented follow-up (touch rootfs-transform.sh + drop the 3
#       lines here), deferred to avoid disturbing the committed base. usr/br/bin/
#       busybox is the source-built static busybox CLI applet binary (the
#       OpenRC overlay ships its own /bin/busybox.openrc) — same disposition.
#
#  (iii) MONOLITHIC-BLOB-ONLY (post-build strip is the ONLY option): EVERYTHING
#        else below — samba, Tor, ookla, openvpn, ipsec/strongswan, wireguard.ko,
#        the AiCloud/lighttpd/webdav cluster, minidlna/mt-daapd + media libs,
#        netatalk/AFP, sqlite3/jq CLIs, the DPI stack (wred/dcd/libshn_*), the
#        stock /www tree + httpd/httpds. None is a Buildroot package; all are
#        inside the proprietary gt-be98-rootfs blob. This list stays the SAFETY
#        NET for them. NOTHING was pruned from it (no source removal supersedes
#        any (iii) entry).
# ===========================================================================

# --- /usr/br staging cruft (~5.97MB xz) -------------------------------------
# KEPT (NOT listed): usr/br/sbin/dropbearmulti, usr/br/libexec/sftp-server,
#                    usr/br/bin/scp, usr/br/bin/sftp  (the SSH/SFTP channel)
usr/br/bin/openssl
usr/br/bin/ssh
usr/br/bin/ssh-keygen
usr/br/bin/busybox

# --- samba (~2.74MB) --------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: libsmbclient.so* surviving referrer after this strip is liblightsql.so,
# whose only consumers (mod_aicloud_auth/aidisk_access/smbdav/webdav) are ALL
# removed below, so liblightsql is orphaned and the dangling dep is inert.
usr/sbin/samba_multicall
usr/lib/libsmbclient.so
usr/lib/libsmbclient.so.0
usr/sbin/sambaclient
sbin/write_smb_conf

